<main id="main" class="article-page feature-page"><header class="article-hero"><p class="eyebrow">FinOpsWay features</p><h1>Databricks Serverless Cluster Costs</h1><p class="article-standfirst">See serverless DBU usage in context with the workload, performance mode and reporting period.</p></header><div class="article-body"><figure><picture><img src="/img/examples/serverless.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="FinOpsWay serverless cluster usage view with DBU totals next to the workload, performance mode and reporting period." /></picture><figcaption>FinOpsWay shows serverless DBU totals beside a workload, with the reporting period and performance mode in view.</figcaption></figure><h2 id="cost-context">How is serverless compute billed?</h2><p>Databricks manages the infrastructure for serverless compute. Usage is billed in DBUs and the applicable SKU depends on the workload, such as notebooks, jobs or pipelines.</p><p>Use the billing system table to review serverless usage. Multiple records can belong to one workload, so compare the summed DBUs for the same period.</p><section class="pricing-in-feature" aria-labelledby="serverless-rates-title"><h2 id="serverless-rates-title">Published serverless compute rates</h2><p>Public reference rate in USD per DBU. Serverless infrastructure is included in the DBU rate. The final rate depends on cloud, region, plan and contract.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="pricing-table" role="table"><thead role="rowgroup"><tr role="row"><th scope="col">Compute model</th><th scope="col">Cloud</th><th scope="col">Cloud infrastructure</th><th scope="col">Published compute rate</th></tr></thead><tbody role="rowgroup"><tr role="row"><td>Serverless compute</td><td><span class="pricing-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Cloud</span>AWS, Azure, GCP</td><td><span class="pricing-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Cloud infrastructure</span>Included in DBU rate</td><td><span class="pricing-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Published compute rate</span>$0.75 / DBU</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note">Public reference rate checked October 6, 2026. Use the billing SKU in your workspace for the exact applicable price.</p><p class="pricing-region-note">Prices shown for <span class="pricing-region">US East (AWS us-east-1)</span><a href="https://www.databricks.com/product/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View official Databricks pricing</a>.</p></section><h2 id="workflow">How to review serverless usage</h2><ol class="feature-steps"><li><a href="/onboarding/">Connect FinOpsWay</a> and open the related Databricks workload.</li><li>Read DBU usage and the reporting period.</li><li>Compare similar workloads and periods before changing performance settings.</li></ol><aside class="feature-advice" aria-labelledby="serverless-advice-title"><span class="feature-advice-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span><div><h3 id="serverless-advice-title">Use tags for cost attribution</h3><p>Apply serverless usage policies to pass team or environment tags into billing data.</p></div></aside><h2 id="questions">Common questions</h2><h3>Can serverless usage appear after a workload ends?</h3><p>Yes. Billing data can arrive later, so check freshness before comparing recent runs.</p><h3>Can I use one DBU rate for every serverless workload?</h3><p>No. The SKU and rate vary by workload type, cloud and region.</p><p class="feature-limits">Billing data can lag. Check the reported period and freshness.</p></div><?php include __DIR__ . '/../../includes/feature-sidebar.php'; ?></main>
